----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. WHY THIS STAGE HAD TO BE BUILT FIRST
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The in-tree loader cannot supply a real weight tensor:

  src/deep2/GGUFLoader.cpp  = 35 bytes  ("// STUB: src/deep2/GGUFLoader.cpp")
  emptied by commit 964eed96f "Delete 1006 stub .cpp files"
  no CMake target anywhere in the repo builds a GGUF-reading probe

So EVERY quantisation measurement in this project to date was made on synthetic
Gaussian weights. That was the single largest caveat on the sweep's negative
result, stated explicitly in its own receipt: "inputs are Gaussian, which is the
WRONG distribution for this question... a real-data version could disagree."

It did not disagree.


