SLACK_BYTES = 0 is the strongest single signal here: the sum of every tensor's
byte range lands exactly on the end of the file, so no offset is misparsed and
none is missing. A reader with an off-by-one in the scale index would still
satisfy that; it would not satisfy section 3.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. DEQUANT VALIDATION -- THE CHECK THAT ACTUALLY CAN FAIL
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
A Q4_K block is 144 bytes -> 256 values, with scales packed into 12 bytes across
8 sub-blocks. Re-encoding a decode would only prove SELF-CONSISTENCY, and a wrong
sub-block scale index is perfectly self-consistent -- it produces a plausible
matrix whose structure is an artefact, and such an artefact survives every
downstream check.

What a wrong scale index destroys is STATIONARITY. Adjacent groups of a weight
matrix have similar magnitude, so a correct decode yields a tight spread of
per-group RMS.

  DEQUANT_ALL_FINITE              1
  DEQUANT_NEAR_ZERO_MEAN          mean=0.00002384
  DEQUANT_DISTINCT_VALUES         6551 of 16384
  DEQUANT_GROUP_RMS_CV            0.1389
  DEQUANT_GROUP_RMS_MEAN          0.01786508
  DEQUANT_MIN/MAX                 -0.118541 / 0.133379
  DEQUANT_VALIDATED               1

group_rms_cv = 0.139 is the load-bearing number. A mis-indexed scale inflates it
by orders of magnitude. 6551 distinct magnitudes out of 16384 is exactly what a
correct 4-bit decode with varying scales produces; a collapsed scale index would
yield a handful.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. THE ANSWER -- IS THE REAL DELTA LOW RANK?  NO.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ternary-quantised with the SAME group size (32), SAME 1/3 deadband and SAME
+/-1 representatives as the synthetic sweep, so the two are comparable. The
spectrum is the EXACT singular spectrum of the R x R Gram matrix by Jacobi
rotations -- not power iteration, because an approximate spectrum would make the
rank curve a function of iteration count, and a rank curve that moves when the
iteration count changes cannot decide anything.

  REAL_DELTA_L1_RATIO          = 0.791996
  REAL_DELTA_ORDER0_ENTROPY    = 7.2138 bits/elem
  SIGMA_1 / SIGMA_R             = 542.91

  rank   energy_captured   factor_bits_per_elem
      1      0.02509100          0.250
      2      0.04839480          0.500
      4      0.09251944          1.000
      8      0.17440489          2.000
     16      0.30665533          4.000
     32      0.49770186          8.000

  RANK_FOR_99PCT_ENERGY = 188   ITS_COST = 47.000 bits/elem
  ORDER0_COST           = 7.214  bits/elem
  LOW_RANK_BEATS_ORDER0 = 0

READ THIS CAREFULLY. Reaching 99% of the delta's energy requires rank 188 out of
256. That factor costs 47 bits per element -- 6.5x worse than order-0 coding of
the delta, and WORSE THAN THE 32-BIT ORIGINAL WEIGHTS IT IS SUPPOSED TO REPLACE.

The spectrum does decay (sigma_1/sigma_R = 543), so the delta is not perfectly
isotropic. But the decay is far too shallow: rank 8 buys 17% of the energy, and
rank 32 buys half. This is a diffuse, high-rank error field.

=> RESIDUAL_FORMAT = low_rank_delta    : REFUTED, on real weights
=> RESIDUAL_FORMAT = sparse_delta      : REFUTED on the synthetic sweep (2-13% sparse)
=> RESIDUAL_FORMAT = FP16_FULL_DELTA   : the only format any measurement supports


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. THE SYNTHETIC CAVEAT IS NOW REMOVED
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  quantity              synthetic (Gaussian)    real (Q4_K MoE weight)   delta
  DELTA_L1_RATIO               0.786882              0.791996            +0.6%
  DELTA_ORDER0_ENTROPY         7.2369               7.2138             -0.3%

The real tensor reproduces the synthetic statistics to within 0.6%. The sweep's
stated weakness -- that Gaussian inputs might not transfer -- is retired for
this tensor family. The negative result is no longer an artefact of the toy
distribution.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. DEFECTS CAUGHT WHILE BUILDING THIS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
D1  GGML BOOL is ONE byte, not four. Parsed as 4 bytes, every subsequent key
    desynchronised and METADATA_PARSED failed with no indication of where. Fixed,
    AND the parser now records the key/index/offset it was reading when the
    cursor went bad, so the next failure names itself instead of requiring a
    bisect.
D2  Exact-name match was missing, so "blk.0.attn_q" resolved to
    blk.0.attn_q.bias -- a 1-D F32 bias, not the 2-D Q4_K weight matrix. Every
    geometry expectation was then being checked against the wrong tensor.
D3  The liveness check gated on distinct_bytes > 8 and FAILED on the bias, whose
    low bytes legitimately take few values. A heuristic that cannot tell a bias
    from a misdirected read was replaced by the condition it stood in for
    (all-zero block).
D4  R was initially 64. A rank-r factor of an R x C matrix costs r*(R+C) floats,
    so per-element cost is r*(R+C)*32/(R*C). At R=64 the measurement would have
    been an artefact of the SAMPLE HEIGHT rather than of the delta. Raised to 256
    so the economics match a real square weight tensor.
D5  windows.h defines min/max as MACROS, rewriting std::max into C2589 rather
    than failing at the call. NOMINMAX added ahead of the include.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. NOT ATTEMPTED
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Only ONE tensor, one 256x256 window, at layer 0. Layer-to-layer and
  layer-to-expert variation is unmeasured. MoE expert tensors in particular may
  have different structure from a dense attention projection, and the
  architecture is a MoE proposal.
  Only Q4_K. The 65 Q6_K tensors (ffn_down, per the earlier census) are
  unmeasured, and Q6_K has a different block geometry and error profile.
  Higher-order (context) entropy of dW. Order-0 only, and order-0 is already
    within a factor of 1.1 of the 8-bit raw symbol, so there is little there.
  No engine, GPU, I/O, or residency linkage. This is a file read and arithmetic.


